  "goodToKnow": "Die Geldpolitik is monetary policy, managing money supply and interest rates. In the euro area, it's run by the EZB in Frankfurt. Germans, shaped by hyperinflation memories, have often criticised loose monetary policy and negative interest rates (Negativzinsen) that hurt savers in the 2010s. Fiscal policy (taxes and spending) is die Fiskalpolitik or Finanzpolitik. Geldpolitisch means monetary. It has no plural."
